ference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/state.json" "file_sha256" "503b43f9f4955871e7f63209fafc3758f644445e8bbe28d5b724ad8c7c53138b" "basis" 1077 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130523" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The  $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}10x+25y=15 \\\\ 12x+3y=-6\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying both equations in the system, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x+5y=3 \\\\ 4x+y=-2.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/state.json" "file_sha256" "503b43f9f4955871e7f63209fafc3758f644445e8bbe28d5b724ad8c7c53138b" "basis" 1077 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130523" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "da2609ed45aa31cb1d9766990d31695403480cac39b14c0e2dbfd6af4687a711" "basis" 1077 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130523" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/state.json" "file_sha256" "503b43f9f4955871e7f63209fafc3758f644445e8bbe28d5b724ad8c7c53138b" "basis" 1077 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130523" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}10x+25y=-15 \\\\ 12x+3y=6\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/state.json" "file_sha256" "503b43f9f4955871e7f63209fafc3758f644445e8bbe28d5b724ad8c7c53138b" "basis" 1077 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130523" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}10x+25y=-15 \\\\ 12x+6y=3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/state.json" "file_sha256" "503b43f9f4955871e7f63209fafc3758f644445e8bbe28d5b724ad8c7c53138b" "basis" 1077 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130523" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}10x+5y=-15 \\\\ 12x+3y=6\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/state.json" "file_sha256" "503b43f9f4955871e7f63209fafc3758f644445e8bbe28d5b724ad8c7c53138b" "basis" 1077 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130523" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x+5y=15 \\\\ 4x+y=-6\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/state.json" "file_sha256" "503b43f9f4955871e7f63209fafc3758f644445e8bbe28d5b724ad8c7c53138b" "basis" 1077 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130523" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x+5y=3 \\\\ 4x+y=-2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/state.json" "file_sha256" "503b43f9f4955871e7f63209fafc3758f644445e8bbe28d5b724ad8c7c53138b" "basis" 1077 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4505" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x=5 \\\\ -5x+6y=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/example-4505.json" "file_sha256" "cb485af6a14777b4b75042c5ecb5a74d3ec1ca91a996e7778067a41b3f9eb9db" "basis" 1077 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4505" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write the system so that both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation. The variable $y$ does not appear in the first equation, but this just means its coefficient is $0.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+0y=5 \\\\ -5x+6y=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/example-4505.json" "file_sha256" "cb485af6a14777b4b75042c5ecb5a74d3ec1ca91a996e7778067a41b3f9eb9db" "basis" 1077 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-5y=-3x \\\\ 6+x=-2+y\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/example-4506.json" "file_sha256" "09e29b750be86353c8cddb12ea58e7dd22417a827bd95f7b0e09cc30e2d83fd3" "basis" 1077 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we organize the system so that it’s in the correct order:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}3x-5y=0 \\\\ x-y=-8.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/example-4506.json" "file_sha256" "09e29b750be86353c8cddb12ea58e7dd22417a827bd95f7b0e09cc30e2d83fd3" "basis" 1077 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4507" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the system of equations represented by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}10 & -15 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/example-4507.json" "file_sha256" "6469b766629a6a7254544167d7755db429c3bd7d3d874ebd5ab613f849e785ab" "basis" 1077 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4507" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The  $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}10x-15y=5 \\\\ 1x+0y=-2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying both equations in the system, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y=1 \\\\ x=-2.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/example-4507.json" "file_sha256" "6469b766629a6a7254544167d7755db429c3bd7d3d874ebd5ab613f849e785ab" "basis" 1077 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994130/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-71800" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-y=7 \\\\ x+y=-3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/state.json" "file_sha256" "831802528188d36ef82ae49e4ffda0395c095e50b275fce66ca43338fae150b2"} {"question" "q-71800" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation, all the variables are on the left-hand side, and all the constants are on the right-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-y=7 \\\\ x+y=-3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/state.json" "file_sha256" "831802528188d36ef82ae49e4ffda0395c095e50b275fce66ca43338fae150b2"} {"question" "q-71800" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7ea1163e341b5e6aac8ef223fe0209b2528e217ab8154ceb205e741d31a9c62b"} {"question" "q-71800" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/state.json" "file_sha256" "831802528188d36ef82ae49e4ffda0395c095e50b275fce66ca43338fae150b2"} {"question" "q-71800" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/state.json" "file_sha256" "831802528188d36ef82ae49e4ffda0395c095e50b275fce66ca43338fae150b2"} {"question" "q-71800" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/state.json" "file_sha256" "831802528188d36ef82ae49e4ffda0395c095e50b275fce66ca43338fae150b2"} {"question" "q-317500" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-6y=4 \\\\ 3x+5y\\,=-7\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits representation using matrices is\n\n| |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $5$ |  | |  |  |  | |  | $x$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $y$ |  | | $=$ | |  | $4$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-4}} |  | |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $5$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $x$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $y$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $4$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |  |\n\n." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/state.json" "file_sha256" "831802528188d36ef82ae49e4ffda0395c095e50b275fce66ca43338fae150b2"} {"question" "q-317500" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write the system so that both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation. \nThe variable $x$ does not appear in the first equation, but this just means its coefficient is $0.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}0x-6y=4 \\\\ 3x+5y\\,=-7\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -6 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & -6 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/state.json" "file_sha256" "831802528188d36ef82ae49e4ffda0395c095e50b275fce66ca43338fae150b2"} {"question" "q-317500" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7ea1163e341b5e6aac8ef223fe0209b2528e217ab8154ceb205e741d31a9c62b"} {"question" "q-317500" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/stat