/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/state.json" "file_sha256" "831802528188d36ef82ae49e4ffda0395c095e50b275fce66ca43338fae150b2"} {"question" "q-317540" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/state.json" "file_sha256" "831802528188d36ef82ae49e4ffda0395c095e50b275fce66ca43338fae150b2"} {"question" "q-317540" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/state.json" "file_sha256" "831802528188d36ef82ae49e4ffda0395c095e50b275fce66ca43338fae150b2"} {"question" "q-317563" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the system of equations represented by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}8 & -4 \\\\ -6 & 12\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ -18\\end{aligned}]?\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system of equations is\n\n| { | {{field-1}} | $=$ | $\\,4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| {{field-2}} | $=$ | $\\,\\,3.$ |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/state.json" "file_sha256" "831802528188d36ef82ae49e4ffda0395c095e50b275fce66ca43338fae150b2"} {"question" "q-317563" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The $2\\times 2$ matrix encodes the coefficients of $x$ and $y$, and the $2\\times 1$ vector on the right gives the constants, so the system is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}8x-4y=16 \\\\ -6x+12y=-18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the first equation by $4$ and the second by $-6$ gives the simplified system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-y=4 \\\\ x-2y=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich matches the entries shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/state.json" "file_sha256" "831802528188d36ef82ae49e4ffda0395c095e50b275fce66ca43338fae150b2"} {"question" "q-317563" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7ea1163e341b5e6aac8ef223fe0209b2528e217ab8154ceb205e741d31a9c62b"} {"question" "q-317563" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/state.json" "file_sha256" "831802528188d36ef82ae49e4ffda0395c095e50b275fce66ca43338fae150b2"} {"question" "q-317563" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2x-y"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/state.json" "file_sha256" "831802528188d36ef82ae49e4ffda0395c095e50b275fce66ca43338fae150b2"} {"question" "q-317563" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/state.json" "file_sha256" "831802528188d36ef82ae49e4ffda0395c095e50b275fce66ca43338fae150b2"} {"question" "q-317563" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x-2y"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/state.json" "file_sha256" "831802528188d36ef82ae49e4ffda0395c095e50b275fce66ca43338fae150b2"} {"question" "q-71854" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the system of equations represented by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 12\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -15\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/state.json" "file_sha256" "831802528188d36ef82ae49e4ffda0395c095e50b275fce66ca43338fae150b2"} {"question" "q-71854" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The  $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}0x-y=0 \\\\ -3x+12y=-15.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying both equations in the system, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}y=0 \\\\ x-4y=5.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/state.json" "file_sha256" "831802528188d36ef82ae49e4ffda0395c095e50b275fce66ca43338fae150b2"} {"question" "q-71854" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7ea1163e341b5e6aac8ef223fe0209b2528e217ab8154ceb205e741d31a9c62b"} {"question" "q-71854" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/state.json" "file_sha256" "831802528188d36ef82ae49e4ffda0395c095e50b275fce66ca43338fae150b2"} {"question" "q-71854" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x=0 \\\\ x-3y=5\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "\\be