/state.json" "file_sha256" "831802528188d36ef82ae49e4ffda0395c095e50b275fce66ca43338fae150b2"} {"question" "q-317570" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4x-5y"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/state.json" "file_sha256" "831802528188d36ef82ae49e4ffda0395c095e50b275fce66ca43338fae150b2"} {"question" "q-317570" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/state.json" "file_sha256" "831802528188d36ef82ae49e4ffda0395c095e50b275fce66ca43338fae150b2"} {"question" "q-317570" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3x+2y"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/state.json" "file_sha256" "831802528188d36ef82ae49e4ffda0395c095e50b275fce66ca43338fae150b2"} {"question" "q-317583" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the system of equations represented by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]?\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system of equations is\n\n| { | {{field-1}} | $=$ | $10$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| {{field-2}} | $=$ | $\\,\\,-7.$ |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/state.json" "file_sha256" "831802528188d36ef82ae49e4ffda0395c095e50b275fce66ca43338fae150b2"} {"question" "q-317583" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The  $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}5x+0y=10 \\\\ -3x+2y=-7\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying both equations in the system, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}5x=10 \\\\ -3x+2y=-7\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/state.json" "file_sha256" "831802528188d36ef82ae49e4ffda0395c095e50b275fce66ca43338fae150b2"} {"question" "q-317583" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7ea1163e341b5e6aac8ef223fe0209b2528e217ab8154ceb205e741d31a9c62b"} {"question" "q-317583" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/state.json" "file_sha256" "831802528188d36ef82ae49e4ffda0395c095e50b275fce66ca43338fae150b2"} {"question" "q-317583" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/state.json" "file_sha256" "831802528188d36ef82ae49e4ffda0395c095e50b275fce66ca43338fae150b2"} {"question" "q-317583" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/state.json" "file_sha256" "831802528188d36ef82ae49e4ffda0395c095e50b275fce66ca43338fae150b2"} {"question" "q-317583" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3x+2y"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/state.json" "file_sha256" "831802528188d36ef82ae49e4ffda0395c095e50b275fce66ca43338fae150b2"} {"question" "e-4505" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x=5 \\\\ -5x+6y=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/example-4505.json" "file_sha256" "07c9d88319c24322cf0dc9acc05fefed1932be7207513eec7902c33b5fedad6d"} {"question" "e-4505" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write the system so that both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation. The variable $y$ does not appear in the first equation, but this just means its coefficient is $0.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+0y=5 \\\\ -5x+6y=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/assets/cdadd8a9c68f58c4d8434e658d4acffeba524850f361fcd3d6fe3524b3d781a1.png)\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/assets/35104266eb5a086bef0536640ec1310532cc136a251049a1adcfe4418ef0ef89.png)\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/assets/aa4de061ca95088763e7e5fec289dbd2e5bd298e8986ef6660617ea0ba227821.png)\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/assets/10781c0f9183c793e3f2de287ede937e764d942767ecc9b64942dc338c1e1307.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/example-4505.json" "file_sha256" "07c9d88319c24322cf0dc9acc05fefed1932be7207513eec7902c33b5fedad6d"} {"question" "e-4506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-5y=-3x \\\\ 6+x=-2+y\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/example-4506.json" "file_sha256" "58f4adefd06041374f590b22905744fa06ae897f52110ee8f75481f22bc56e56"} {"question" "e-4506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we organize the system so that it’s in the correct order:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}3x-5y=0 \\\\ x-y=-8.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/assets/648952bc6e093c08ff29215fce21fe115ab81e9fc3d8b423772123eae31237f3.png)\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/assets/c1f203be0770c298d9c2c75ccfbfb30354cb314ed75c8b05f6639e5633ca7442.png)\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/assets/aa4de061ca95088763e7e5fec289dbd2e5bd298e8986ef6660617ea0ba227821.png)\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/assets/75aed8c54a2ec274def967802cbd3b67d0fad3358e676b02cf52e1e8d2cbe0d7.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/example-4506.json" "file_sha256" "58f4adefd06041374f590b22905744fa06ae897f52110ee8f75481f22bc56e56"} {"question" "e-4507" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the system of equations represented by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/assets/6f0ddb43928e0d9f52ca2fe0f0ab578adfa986cba8179746bd34a50a1a7c506b.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/example-4507.json" "file_sha256" "5d6399d3ef4fab60603554d9eb1abf21ff2c063d38f9e8fd98725403b9e1a39d"} {"question" "e-4507" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The  $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}10x-15y=5 \\\\ 1x+0y=-2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying both equations in the system, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y=1 \\\\ x=-2.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/example-4507.json" "file_sha256" "5d6399d3ef4fab60603554d9eb1abf21ff2c063d38f9e8fd98725403b9e1a39d"}] "usage" {"q-130523" [] "q-317530" [] "q-317506" [] "e-4505" [] "q-317500" [] "e-4506" [] "e-4507" []} "basis" 1760 "retractions" [[17592186114979 :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation. The variable $y$ does not appear in the first equation, but this just means its coefficient is $0.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+0y=5 \\\\ -5x+6y=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$"] [17592186114980 :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that it’s in the correct order:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}3x-5y=0 \\\\ x-y=-8.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$"] [17592186114981 :question/problem "What is the system of equations represented by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}10 & -15 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186285569 17592186285570 17592186285571 17592186285572 17592186285573 17592186285600 17592186285602 17592186285604 17592186285606 17592186285609 17592186285610 17592186285612 17592186285614 17592186285616 17592186285638 17592186285640 17592186285642 17592186285644] "immutable_fields" [[17592186285568 :answer-field/correct] [17592186285568 :answer-field/id] [17592186285568 :answer-field/key] [17592186285568 :answer-field/type] [17592186285599 :answer-field/correct] [17592186285599 :answer-field/id] [17592186285599 :answer-field/key] [17592186285599 :answer-field/type] [17592186285601 :answer-field/correct] [17592186285601 :answer-field/id] [17592186285601 :answer-field/key] [17592186285601 :answer-field/type] [17592186285603 :answer-field/correct] [17592186285603 :answer-field/id] [17592186285603 :answer-field/key] [175